  "verbalization": "Jerantinine B appears to have a shared target relationship with Carboxylesterase 2 through a series of intermediaries, including Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and other compounds such as 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside and Isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside. These intermediates are all known targets of Carboxylesterase 2, suggesting a potential pathway where Jerantinine B may modulate the activity of Carboxylesterase 2 through the activation of these compounds. The evidence suggests that Jerantinine B may act as a ligand or activator of Thioredoxin, which in turn may influence the activity of Carboxylesterase 2. This mechanism is supported by the high scores in the visible paths, indicating a strong and consistent relationship across different compounds. The integration of these findings implies that Jerantinine B could be involved in a broader regulatory network that affects Carboxylesterase 2 activity, potentially through a series of molecular interactions that are not yet fully elucidated.",
